#: freeports_dev.ci.readers:1 of
msgid "Turning each tool's own JSON into the one record shape the gate reads."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.readers:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Every measurement tool here answers in its own dialect: ``cargo llvm-"
"cov`` nests totals under ``data[0].totals.lines.percent``, "
"``coverage.py`` puts them at ``totals.percent_covered``, rustdoc gives a "
"map of files to ``{total, with_docs}`` with an ``#ALL#`` row that is a "
"total and not a file. Knowledge of those dialects lives here and nowhere "
"else."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.readers:8 of
msgid ""
"The alternative was a shell fragment per tool inside a Makefile recipe, "
"and it is worth saying why that was rejected: those fragments cannot be "
"tested. A reader in this module is exercised by a fixture that is a "
"captured output of the real tool, so the day ``llvm-cov`` moves a key the"
" suite says so — instead of a Makefile quietly producing an empty string,"
" the gate reading it as zero, and a commit being refused for a reason "
"nobody can find."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.readers:14 of
msgid ""
"Each reader takes parsed JSON and returns a "
":class:`~freeports_dev.ci.report.Measurement`. None of them runs "
"anything: what produced the file is the caller's business, which is what "
"makes them testable without the tool installed."
msgstr ""

